.TH OSHOTPM 1 "2026-10-17" "oshot" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
oshotpm \- plugin manager for oshot
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oshotpm
.RB [ \-h | \-V ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B oshotpm
installs, updates and removes plugins for
.BR oshot (1).
Plugins are shared libraries described by an \fIoshot\-plugin.toml\fR manifest.
A \fIrepository\fR is everything one manifest describes; each plugin in it has an
\fIID\fR like \fBio.github.user.plugin\fR.
Changes apply the next time oshot starts.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR search " [\fB\-v\fR] [\fIWORD\fR]..."
List the plugins in the plugin index, or the ones matching every \fIWORD\fR.
\fB\-v\fR adds every version, the owners, the license and the homepage.
.TP
.BR install " [\fB\-f\fR] [\fB\-y\fR] \fISOURCE\fR..."
Install the plugins from each \fISOURCE\fR: a plugin ID from the plugin index (its
newest version that works here, prebuilt for this computer when available, checked
against the index's SHA\-256), a git URL (cloned, then built with the manifest's
build steps), a local folder with a manifest (built in place), or a prebuilt archive
(\fI.zip\fR, \fI.tar.gz\fR/\fI.tgz\fR, \fI.tar.xz\fR/\fI.txz\fR).
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR reinstalls a repository that is already installed.
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR answers every question with its default.
.TP
.BR update " [\fB\-y\fR]"
Install newer versions of the plugins from the plugin index, warning about withdrawn
ones, and fetch every repository installed from a git URL and rebuild the ones that
changed.
.TP
.BI uninstall " NAME" ...
Uninstall the plugin with the ID \fINAME\fR, or the repository named \fINAME\fR with
all its plugins. Their settings are deleted too.
.TP
.BI enable " PLUGIN" ...
.TQ
.BI disable " PLUGIN" ...
Enable or disable plugins, given by ID or as \fIREPOSITORY\fB/\fIplugin name\fR.
.TP
.BR list " [\fB\-v\fR]"
List the installed repositories and plugins; \fB\-v\fR adds authors, licenses,
platforms and library paths.
.TP
.B gen\-manifest
Write a commented template \fIoshot\-plugin.toml\fR in the current folder.
.TP
.BI help " [COMMAND]"
Show the help of \fICOMMAND\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and other information about the build.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OSHOT_SDK
The plugin SDK (a folder with \fIinclude/oshot/oshot_plugin.h\fR) passed to plugin
builds, instead of the one next to oshot.
.TP
.B OSHOT_PLUGIN_INDEX
URL of the plugin index (any URL curl takes), instead of
https://toni500github.github.io/oshot\-plugin\-index/index.toml.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Don't color the output.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/oshot/plugins/
Installed plugins, one folder per ID with the library and its \fIconfig.toml\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.config/oshot/plugins/state.toml
What is installed.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/oshotpm/
Clones of the repositories installed from git, and the last downloaded plugin index.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if anything failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
oshotpm search translate
oshotpm install io.github.user.translate
oshotpm install https://github.com/user/oshot\-plugins
oshotpm install ./my\-plugin
oshotpm disable io.github.user.translate
oshotpm uninstall oshot\-plugins
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR oshot (1)
